#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""deaddrop - a tile-based secret agent adventure of the 1960s, in Python + Tk.

Standard library only.  The engine is Penultimate's (one adventurer, a map
of squares, people to talk to by keyword, shops, places below), and the rules
are those of the classic secret agent roleplaying game of 1983: five
characteristics, skills whose Primary Chance is multiplied by an Ease Factor,
a D100 roll read for its Quality, Hero Points that turn the impossible into
the merely unlikely, and a Wound Level chart in place of hit points.

London, Friday the 1st of October, 1965.  The courier carrying the arming
package of HESPERUS, NATO's new orbital rocket, has been found dead in a
Brussels hotel, and the package is gone.  ORCUS, the Organisation for
Revenge, Coercion, Usurpation and Subversion, means to fire it at midnight
on Sunday the 10th, and to blind both East and West at once.  ORCUS runs
its operations through cells in the great cities of the world; four of them
hold strips of microfilm cut from the plan.  Find the strips, find the base,
and stop the launch.

Every new game deals a new mission: four cities of eight (Paris, Rome,
Berlin, Moscow, New York, Hong Kong, Istanbul and Tokyo), each with its own
map, landmarks, people and music; a new base, four new cell chiefs, and a
Chairman of ORCUS who is one of six of the international set.  The game is
saved to ~/.deaddrop.json whenever you change place and when you quit.

Agents: choose a background and roll characteristics (STR, DEX, WIL, PER,
INT, from 5 to 15).  A skill's Primary Chance is a characteristic, or the
average of two, plus its Skill Level; a task's Success Chance is that times
an Ease Factor (5 for an ordinary task, less for hard ones), and the D100
roll's Quality, 1 (Excellent) to 4 (Acceptable), says how well it went.
A Quality 1 earns a Hero Point; Hero Points rescue failures and turn
bullets aside.  Wounds add up, Light to Medium to Heavy to Incapacitated to
Killed, and each makes every task harder until it heals.

Keys: arrows or WASD move, Space waits (and takes cover), E searches, F
fires and R reloads, G uses a gadget, U uses or readies something, I shows
your dossier, P the mission file, J the journal, M the map, ? help.

The tiles are drawn by the code below: no image files.  deaddrop --selftest
builds every map, room, level and tune of a few missions without a window.

App bundle (macOS):  deaddrop --build-app [DIR]   builds deaddrop.app
                     deaddrop --icon-png SIZE [OUT.png]
"""

